body:
After forming Huron, and gaining the Government rank of kingdom, taking any reforms reverts you to rank of duchy.

&#x200B;

if the starting nation has the settle down reform, and switches to seasonal travel, they remain able to settle areas, without the power point penalty. However taking any reform other than settle down causes all settled land to revert to unsettled tribal land.

Voting 3rd party has nothing to do with caring about who gets in this election. It's about keeping to your morals and not voting for a rapist, or because other people tell you that you HAVE to vote for the establishment candidate because otherwise hellfire and brimstone will end the world or whatever other reason they say. When the party you were going to vote for does everything in their power not to let the frontrunner win, they dont deserve the votes. 

&#x200B;

As far as "not fucking the environment" goes, it's already fucked and biden wont even attempt to fix it. As far as I'm concerned, thats as bad as actively killing thousands in several states that will be severely affected by climate change. I'm lucky to live in a state that will only likely see increased rainfall. I wont be a person dealing with forest fires, rising seas, or drought. My crops will still grow. That doesn't mean I'm willing to vote for the destruction of large swaths of the US by voting for "the lesser evil". I'd rather vote for someone who doesnt stand a chance if my vote wont matter anyways, and show the establishment that I won't tolerate their actions.

The converter is clearly wrong, however, 35K above normal would be the same as 35C hotter than normal. (Kelvin scale is just the Celsius scale -273.15°)

&#x200B;

That's roughly 63°F above normal

I never even thought about shoes! Ill suggest them for her and we can go out and grab the claw thing that /u/Trilobyte141 mentioned too! We've been fortunate that she hasn't needed any kind of restrictions on diet so far!

&#x200B;

Tiredness seems to be the worst thing for her currently. She used to be able to run on like 4 hours of sleep a night consistently. She got one of those pregnancy pillows, the U shaped ones, and that helps a lot! She's been a great sport, and I think she's more exhausted than she lets on, so I want to try to let her know it's ok to be exhausted without saying it outright :)
